dom NPC or  inanimate object  the teleportation gloves aren't the only  cool things we'll get in for joy though  there's also a healing ring that you can  obtain through the quests the murderous  Geist Magister yarrow will ask you to  confront me go  a missing inmate who's now a grotesque  looking monster yeah he's kind of been  having a bad day and unless you've got a  yarrow flower on you you're gonna have  to fight him for the ring once you have  it though the quest requires you to give  the ring back in order to complete it so  your options are as follows give it back  and have no cool healing ring you doofus  keep it and have a cool healing ring or  give it back kill yarrow and have a cool  healing ring you murderer if you have no  moral compass feel free to kill both at  least we get some nice gear to cover up  that cold cold heart of yours fancy a  fight then the arena is perfect for you  find and talk to new C for the quests  and then enter the arena through the  trapdoor on the ground you'll have to  fight your way through a bunch of  enemies and if you succeed you'll be  deemed the one now as the one you'll be  able to visit a blacksmith to remove  your source collar which actually if you  do it too early could pose a problem for  your character while it's probably the  easiest method to get off the Magisters  that you run into will promptly throw  you in prison afterwards making getting  anything done and town a hassle so maybe  wait till you're almost ready to leave  to do the arena also fun fact if you're  interested in bringing a friend with you  into the arena your friendly co-op  session will eventually turn into a  fight to the death as there can only be  one the one so make sure you decide  amongst yourselves who's gonna be the  one before you actually start  [Laughter]  there's no shortage of cool things to  create into van de original sin - and as  a rule of thumb always pick up and read  as many books as possible not only is  reading good for you but these crafting  books have recipes for spells food and  other helpful items so make sure you  scour Fort Joy high and low for these  now what's an adventure without some  great party members to experience it  with while it's entirely possible to go  it alone you'll definitely want to  recruit some hearty teammates to help  you in your journey and for joy is a  first and most convenient place to do it  the red prints is hard to miss as he's  located outside of Fort joy near the  beach you wash ashore on Beast is also  located on the beach over to the west of  Griffes camp he'll be fixing up a wreck  ship civil can be found stalking the  lizard sting tail you'll first see here  near Griffes camp and afterward she'll  be near sting tales camp which is to the  west of the elf cave low sea is pretty  hard to miss she's right in front of the  fort joy Waypoint shrine and a faun is  equally hard to miss once you enter the  fort you'll hear a commotion over some  thugs harassing an elf and a faun  defending her intervene and then talk to  a fawn and finally Fain's location can  be a little bit tricky and is pretty  easy to miss head north out of Fort joy  follow the path on the right side and  you'll come across a hidden alcove go  through it and you'll find Fane leaning  over a body of course with a healthy  number of party members to choose from  come some hard decisions as well  unfortunately you can only have four  party members at a time which means that  some of them will be left back in fort  joy you can swap them in and out and  give each character a trial run but  sadly you're eventually going to have to  give a few of them the boot you'll also  be able to decide the class of each  party member and if you mess up it'll be  a good long while until you can change  it so think very carefully about your  team's composition we'll have a  character class guide coming up soon so  if you're uncertain about which one to  choose make sure to watch out for that  now if 